# Residual exchange and the moving-plane obstruction

The actual component parabolic and rank-two quotient give invariance of both
residual directions and normalization of L by S. The literal centralizer
residual excludes the second choice, so Y₊ = Y. The orthogonal action then
identifies the component residuals with the definite-plane residuals and
proves their exchange and the moving-plane geometry in either orientation.

The component parabolic is exactly the stabilizer of this plane. Its placement
in the natural layers preserves their common quotient marking. The complete
fifth alternative is excluded using its central-omega clause in the actual
local group. These reductions take the genuine earlier local conclusions and
[V,Y_L] ≠ 1 as inputs; the separate extension proof and case-(4) exclusion
remain with the parent FixedSpaces assembly.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript (1 March 2004),
15.3.23, printed p.1128; C.1.34, printed pp.136–137.
-/
